From 804d71ac53509c002b4ab1e35a0be48f993de610 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marc Aldrich <7917445+MarcAldrich@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 23:03:13 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] xpu-inkling2: Xe2 XMX DPAS prefill/attn, DP4A decode,
 async pipeline

Optimize xpu-inkling2 for Intel Arc Pro B70 (BMG-G31 / Xe2):
- Pipelined async decode via ink2_embed_dev + 2-slot host-pinned event ring (INK2_SYNC=1 fallback).
- Vectorized decode mix3/mix3n, split-K BF16 loop controllers, 0-barrier 1-sg top-8 router_k.
- Hardware DP4A Q8_0 decode with fused 0-barrier warp-shuffle Q8_1 quant (INK2_NODP4A=1 fallback).
- 32-Xe-core 9-wave alignment (KERNEL(64)) on down_nvfp4d, down_q8_dp4a, gemv_conv2s_dp4a.
- Xe2 XMX DPAS prefill (TMAX=256) for Q8_0, NVFP4 (exact E2M1->fp16 unpack), and FlashAttention
  (ink2_attn_b_xmx with 2D block reads), plus dual 128/256-GRF module dispatch (INK2_NOXMX=1 fallback).
- Zero-scratch online-softmax fallback ink2_attn_b enabling up to 384K context on 32 GiB B70.
